Well, the answer is, it's not really wayfinding for us, for patrons of the park. It's really for park employees whose job it is to replace and repair those lamps. Now that you know, you could, like, spin around with a blindfold on, set off in any direction, find a lamp, and know where you are in Central Park, which is pretty cool. And if you love little design stories like that, you're going to find a little design stories like that, you're going to find a lot more when you page through your copy of the 99% Invisible City or listen to the audiobook narrated by our very own Roman Mars. So head to 99PI.org slash book and pick up your preferred format.
